        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0445" n="351" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg351"/>

                <head>No. 260.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vignaud to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 5, 1887</date>.
                        (Received September 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 478.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with Mr. Porter’s request of
                    June 29 (No. 240), I have brought before the French foreign office the case of
                    Mr. J. Oarlin, an American citizen of French origin, who deserted some years ago
                    from a French ship, and who desires now to return to France for the purpose of
                    visiting his aged mother.</p>
                <p>Under date of the 1st instant, Mr. Flourens writes that he has submitted the
                    matter to his colleague of the navy department, and that the desire expressed to
                    him can not be complied with.</p>
                <p>I inclose herewith a copy and a translation of Mr. Flourens’s note.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Vignaud.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d260-a1.xml" xpointer="d260-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
